    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
Since this is a partially-circular region, we use polar
coordinates.  This gives
<me>\int_{0}^{\pi/3}\int_{0}^{4} f(r\cos(\theta),r\sin(\theta))\,r\,dr\,d\theta.</me>




<alert>(b)</alert>
Since this is a rectangular region, we use Cartesian
coordinates.  This gives
<me>\int_{0}^{2}\int_{4}^{7} f(x,y)\,dy\,dx.</me>



</solution>
